{
 "id": "2026-10-20-china-export-curbs-40-technologies",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "China just drafted limits on forty technologies, including AI. What would it block?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "On October sixteenth, China's commerce and science ministries published a draft. It would add forty technologies to the country's export control catalog. Twenty three are in AI, twelve in solar power, and five in biomedicine, including cell and gene therapy."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Fourteen items would be banned outright. Twenty six more would need a government export license. The A.P. reports that core technology of large AI models trained on sensitive national data would be prohibited, along with some agents built for defense."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "The commerce ministry calls the step necessary, citing national security and keeping AI under human control. It is only a draft. Public comments are open until November fifteenth, and the final list may still change before it takes effect."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will China's final list be as strict as this draft? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
